title: Encoded PowerShell Command Execution
id: 8f3a1c92-4d7b-4e15-9a38-2b6c7f0e5d11
status: experimental
description: Detects PowerShell executed with a base64-encoded command argument, commonly used to obfuscate payloads and evade command-line inspection.
references:
    - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059/001/
author: Mohemed Abdulla Irfan
date: 2026-09-15
tags:
    - attack.execution
    - attack.t1059.001
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_img:
        - Image|endswith: '\powershell.exe'
        - Image|endswith: '\pwsh.exe'
    selection_flag:
        CommandLine|contains:
            - ' -enc '
            - ' -encodedcommand '
            - ' -ec '
    condition: all of selection_*
falsepositives:
    - Software deployment and provisioning scripts that encode arguments to avoid shell quoting problems
    - Some monitoring and backup agents invoke encoded PowerShell on a schedule
level: high
